{"id":"34829531471","type":"PushEvent","actor":{"id":82850873,"login":"LMAO-armv8","display_login":"LMAO-armv8","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LMAO-armv8","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82850873?"},"repo":{"id":735914036,"name":"LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q"},"payload":{"repository_id":735914036,"push_id":16642862770,"size":12,"distinct_size":12,"ref":"refs/heads/rebase","head":"b25dd2842bcaef2413db7a06c67034b187aa007f","before":"80ac2912f846c01d702774bb6aa7100ec71e88b9","commits":[{"sha":"e605ecd7c8a38f65759c938a235a1b84f41a744e","author":{"email":"dsaxena@plexity.net","name":"Deepak Saxena"},"message":"[ARM] 2834/1: Remove IXP4xx board-specific map_io routines\n\nPatch from Deepak Saxena\n\nNone of the board-specific map_io routines do anything, so kill them.\n\nSigned-off-by: Deepak Saxena <dsaxena@plexity.net>\nSigned-off-by: Russell King <rmk+kernel@arm.linux.org.uk>","distinct":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q/commits/e605ecd7c8a38f65759c938a235a1b84f41a744e"},{"sha":"bdf82b59c5dcf04bbdbd1938eefca14dd9cb44d3","author":{"email":"dsaxena@plexity.net","name":"Deepak Saxena"},"message":"[ARM] 2836/1: Cleanup IXP4xx GPIO code\n\nPatch from Deepak Saxena\n\nThis patch implements the set_irq_type() hooks for configuring GPIO\nIRQ type and updates all the platforms to use it instead of the\ngpio_line_config() function which is now used to configure input\nvs. output on the pins.\n\nSigned-off-by: Deepak Saxena <dsaxena@plexity.net>\nSigned-off-by: Russell King <rmk+kernel@arm.linux.org.uk>","distinct":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q/commits/bdf82b59c5dcf04bbdbd1938eefca14dd9cb44d3"},{"sha":"d6b0bf213b4be478029b768fcee80058ace7150a","author":{"email":"ben-linux@fluff.org","name":"Ben Dooks"},"message":"[ARM] 2855/1: S3C2410 - add CLKSLOW definitions, and show in init\n\nPatch from Ben Dooks\n\nAdd the definitions for the S3C2410_CLKSLOW registers to\nthe header files, and show the values when the system\nstarts up\n\nSigned-off-by: Ben Dooks <ben-linux@fluff.org>\nSigned-off-by: Russell King <rmk+kernel@arm.linux.org.uk>","distinct":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q/commits/d6b0bf213b4be478029b768fcee80058ace7150a"},{"sha":"01b9c414828d951148a3792237ff3bf6e6debc85","author":{"email":"ben-linux@fluff.org","name":"Ben Dooks"},"message":"[ARM] 2856/1: S3C2440 - show DVS status at startup\n\nPatch from Ben Dooks\n\nShow the state of DVS (Dynamic Voltage Scaling) when\nstarting up on the S3C2440\n\nSigned-off-by: Ben Dooks <ben-linux@fluff.org>\nSigned-off-by: Russell King <rmk+kernel@arm.linux.org.uk>","distinct":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q/commits/01b9c414828d951148a3792237ff3bf6e6debc85"},{"sha":"cb85a502e0c2019d8bc302b011150bd62ecf70ab","author":{"email":"nico@cam.org","name":"Nicolas Pitre"},"message":"[ARM] 2858/1: ARM has sys_fadvise64_64 only\n\nPatch from Nicolas Pitre\n\nThere is no need to define __ARCH_WANT_SYS_FADVISE64 on ARM since it\nonly serves to compile in a compatibility wrapper for sys_fadvise64\nwhich never was tied to any syscall number.\n\nSigned-off-by: Nicolas Pitre <nico@cam.org>\nSigned-off-by: Russell King <rmk+kernel@arm.linux.org.uk>","distinct":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q/commits/cb85a502e0c2019d8bc302b011150bd62ecf70ab"},{"sha":"3e88a579d05e1bb6c51d88f0936e372895edb8ff","author":{"email":"rpurdie@rpsys.net","name":"Richard Purdie"},"message":"[ARM] 2861/1: PXA: Add some extra pxa27x register definitions\n\nPatch from Richard Purdie\n\nAdd some extra pxa27x register definitions needed for the Sharp\nSL-C3000 (Spitz).\n\nSigned-off-by: Richard Purdie <rpurdie@rpsys.net>\nSigned-off-by: Russell King <rmk+kernel@arm.linux.org.uk>","distinct":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q/commits/3e88a579d05e1bb6c51d88f0936e372895edb8ff"},{"sha":"083bc6b3c9b52b5998cc49d4aa2f8f15c2e84e6b","author":{"email":"dsaxena@plexity.net","name":"Deepak Saxena"},"message":"[ARM] 2853/1: Make alloc_init_supersection() work with 36-bit mappings\n\nPatch from Deepak Saxena\n\nWorking on adding support for 36-bit static mappings for ARMv6 and\nIntel's XSC3 core and noticed that alloc_init_supersection currently\nincrements the phys addr by 1MB on each of the 16 iterations and then\nforces alignment to supersection size (16MB).  This is really uneeded\nb/c we have already forced the phys address to be 16MB aligned in\ncreate_mapping(). Furthermore, this breaks 36-bit addressing b/c bits\n[23:20] of the PMD contain bits [35:32] of the physical address and\nthe masking causes us to loose those bits thus ending up with an\nincorrect virt -> phys translation.  The other option is to have an\nalloc_init_supersection36.\nTested on Intel IXP2350 CPU with 36-bit static I/O mappings.\n\nSigned-off-by: Deepak Saxena <dsaxena@plexity.net>\nSigned-off-by: Russell King <rmk+kernel@arm.linux.org.uk>","distinct":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q/commits/083bc6b3c9b52b5998cc49d4aa2f8f15c2e84e6b"},{"sha":"3618886f645c2ede45742d3e3d22a96b2ee2f527","author":{"email":"ben-linux@fluff.org","name":"Ben Dooks"},"message":"[ARM] 2857/2: Dynamic tick - fix OOPS if configured and not provided\n\nPatch from Ben Dooks\n\ntimer_dyn_reprogram() fails with an OOPS if the\nconfiguration for CONFIG_NO_IDLE_HZ is enabled, and\nthe system has no support for it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Ben Dooks <ben-linux@fluff.org>\nSigned-off-by: Russell King <rmk+kernel@arm.linux.org.uk>","distinct":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q/commits/3618886f645c2ede45742d3e3d22a96b2ee2f527"},{"sha":"f21ee2d4245293ee6906eb7afd0a701f40e839b9","author":{"email":"stevel@mwwireless.net","name":"Steve Longerbeam"},"message":"[ARM] 2867/2: unaligned ldrd/strd fixups\n\nPatch from Steve Longerbeam\n\nAdds an implementation of unaligned LDRD and STRD fixups.\nAlso fixes a bug where do_alignment() would misinterpret and\nfixup an unaligned LDRD/STRD as LDRH/STRH, causing memory\ncorruption.\nThis is the same as Patch #2867/1, but with minor whitespace\nand comments changes, plus a check for arch-level >= v5TE\nbefore printing ai_dword count in proc_alignment_read().\n\nSigned-off-by: Steve Longerbeam <stevel@mwwireless.net>\nSigned-off-by: Russell King <rmk+kernel@arm.linux.org.uk>","distinct":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q/commits/f21ee2d4245293ee6906eb7afd0a701f40e839b9"},{"sha":"dcb86e8cbd66c5bd6b51a5485ea3ff35bb4ced22","author":{"email":"catalin.marinas@arm.com","name":"Catalin Marinas"},"message":"[ARM] 2868/1: Include linux/cpumask.h in arch/arm/common/gic.c\n\nPatch from Catalin Marinas\n\nMinor compilation error fix.\n\nSigned-off-by: Catalin Marinas <catalin.marinas@arm.com>\nSigned-off-by: Russell King <rmk+kernel@arm.linux.org.uk>","distinct":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q/commits/dcb86e8cbd66c5bd6b51a5485ea3ff35bb4ced22"},{"sha":"147056fb84150966d736fe21fa01d5e0f08e0980","author":{"email":"dvrabel@arcom.com","name":"David Vrabel"},"message":"[ARM] 2869/1: ixp4xx: correct ioread*/iowrite*\n\nPatch from David Vrabel\n\nCorrect the ioread* and iowrite* functions.  In particular, add an offset to the cookie in ioport_map so we can map I/O port ranges starting from 0 (0 is for reporting errors).\n\nSigned-off-by: David Vrabel <dvrabel@arcom.com>\nSigned-off-by: Russell King <rmk+kernel@arm.linux.org.uk>","distinct":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q/commits/147056fb84150966d736fe21fa01d5e0f08e0980"},{"sha":"b25dd2842bcaef2413db7a06c67034b187aa007f","author":{"email":"torvalds@evo.osdl.org","name":"Linus Torvalds"},"message":"Merge HEAD from master.kernel.org:/home/rmk/linux-2.6-arm.git","distinct":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LMAO-armv8/kernel_samsung_r0q/commits/b25dd2842bcaef2413db7a06c67034b187aa007f"}]},"public":true,"created_at":"2024-01-15T12:00:00Z"}
