{"id":"34829531888","type":"IssueCommentEvent","actor":{"id":81654,"login":"gdamjan","display_login":"gdamjan","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81654?"},"repo":{"id":32873313,"name":"systemd/systemd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd"},"payload":{"action":"created","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/issues/30763","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/issues/30763/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/issues/30763/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/issues/30763/events","html_url":"https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/30763","id":2065961076,"node_id":"I_kwDOAfWbYc57JBB0","number":30763,"title":"Cannot assign requested address when bridge configured as DHCP relay","user":{"login":"gdamjan","id":81654,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81654?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan","html_url":"https://github.com/gdamjan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":191919606,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxOTE5MTk2MDY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/labels/bug%20%F0%9F%90%9B","name":"bug 🐛","color":"e11d21","default":false,"description":"Programming errors, that need preferential fixing"},{"id":219549709,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMTk1NDk3MDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/labels/network","name":"network","color":"fad8c7","default":false,"description":null},{"id":239790930,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzk3OTA5MzA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/labels/needs-reporter-feedback%20%E2%9D%93","name":"needs-reporter-feedback ❓","color":"eb6420","default":false,"description":"There's an unanswered question, the reporter needs to answer"},{"id":253688058,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNTM2ODgwNTg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/labels/dhcp","name":"dhcp","color":"bfd4f2","default":false,"description":null},{"id":465645112,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0NjU2NDUxMTI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/labels/cant-reproduce","name":"cant-reproduce","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2024-01-04T16:27:10Z","updated_at":"2024-01-15T12:00:01Z","closed_at":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"body":"### systemd version the issue has been seen with\r\n\r\n255.2-1-arch\r\n\r\n### Used distribution\r\n\r\nArchlinux\r\n\r\n### Linux kernel version used\r\n\r\n6.6.9-arch1-1\r\n\r\n### CPU architectures issue was seen on\r\n\r\nx86_64\r\n\r\n### Component\r\n\r\nsystemd-networkd\r\n\r\n### Expected behaviour you didn't see\r\n\r\nOn my Archlinux host I have a bridge interface configured with systemd-networkd (see configuration below). The bridge is used by virtual machines and nspawn containers (`Bridge=bridge0` in the .nspawn config file). The bridge is also configured as a DHCP server, more specifically as a **DHCP Relay** to my main router.\r\n\r\nThe problem is when the nspawn container is started, and its `vb-machinename` interface is added to the bridge, the bridge becomes `UP` but fails to configure the ip address (see logs below).\r\n\r\nThe problem seems related to the `Relay*` options, since without them, when running the internal dhcp server, there is no problem.\r\n\r\nAlso, a work-around for the issue is if I add `IgnoreCarrierLoss=true` which makes the bridge be `UP` at boot time, before the vb-* interface is added.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Unexpected behaviour you saw\r\n\r\nBridge is not configured with an IP address.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce the problem\r\n\r\nbridge + dhcp relay\r\n```\r\n# /etc/systemd/network/bridge.network \r\n[Match]\r\nName=bridge0\r\n\r\n[Network]\r\nAddress=192.168.2.1/24\r\nDHCPServer=yes\r\nLLDP=yes\r\nMulticastDNS=yes\r\n\r\n\r\n[Link]\r\nRequiredForOnline=no\r\n\r\n[DHCPServer]\r\nRelayTarget=192.168.1.1\r\nRelayAgentRemoteId=string:aabbccdd\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Additional program output to the terminal or log subsystem illustrating the issue\r\n\r\nlogs\r\n```\r\nJan 04 15:44:01 archless systemd-networkd[402]: vb-nixos: Link UP\r\nJan 04 15:44:01 archless systemd-networkd[402]: vb-nixos: Configuring with /usr/lib/systemd/network/80-container-vb.network.\r\nJan 04 15:44:01 archless systemd-networkd[402]: vb-nixos: Gained carrier\r\nJan 04 15:44:01 archless systemd-networkd[402]: bridge0: Gained carrier\r\nJan 04 15:44:01 archless systemd-networkd[402]: bridge0: Could not start DHCP server: Cannot assign requested address\r\nJan 04 15:44:01 archless systemd-networkd[402]: bridge0: Could not process link message: Cannot assign requested address\r\nJan 04 15:44:01 archless systemd-networkd[402]: bridge0: Failed\r\n```\r\n\r\nip status\r\n```\r\n# ip addr show bridge0 ; ip addr show vb-nixos\r\n3: bridge0: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 1500 qdisc noqueue state UP group default qlen 1000\r\n    link/ether 2a:2d:97:73:67:e1 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff\r\n    inet6 fe80::282d:97ff:fe73:67e1/64 scope link proto kernel_ll \r\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\r\n6: vb-nixos@if2: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 1500 qdisc noqueue master bridge0 state UP group default qlen 1000\r\n    link/ether 0e:82:6c:fd:b8:0d brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff link-netnsid 0\r\n```\r\n\r\nalso networkctl\r\n```\r\n# networkctl status bridge0 \r\n● 3: bridge0\r\n                   Link File: /usr/lib/systemd/network/99-default.link\r\n                Network File: /etc/systemd/network/bridge.network\r\n                       State: degraded (failed)\r\n…\r\n```\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/issues/30763/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/issues/30763/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},"comment":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/issues/comments/1892033466","html_url":"https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/30763#issuecomment-1892033466","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/systemd/systemd/issues/30763","id":1892033466,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAfWbYc5wxiO6","user":{"login":"gdamjan","id":81654,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81654?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan","html_url":"https://github.com/gdamjan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gdamjan/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"created_a